<p>Ukraine said it carried out a long-range strike deep inside Russia, hitting an industrial facility in the Udmurt Republic that Kyiv described as a producer of ballistic missiles. Separate reporting also referred to strikes involving the Votkinsk Machine Building Plant in Udmurtia. Russian regional officials reported casualties from the strike in the Udmurt Republic, saying 11 people were wounded and three were hospitalised, according to a Telegram post cited by The Hindu. The latest claims underscore how the war continues to reach far beyond the front lines, with each side describing attacks in terms of military objectives.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/JnmzDMXBIJhe0rrpsX_Kk4CUWvA2WP3sYDkj6bWMuVfkMcDEIAAP69oEuh-FsL0nxL0uuvZwkGKdxW5GGSgWnOrEI6CTdpquFOzrT4TyhDnakjESvy7uQLbtuTh7JhxXz-ms0WtcMTHUZ0Y8xVetvF9ufvJEcIxwDuwflKLSDTeOnlSkZgG_1N_xc7EnKm7OFxe9e8rVWnifpw7Lj_BGrnmY7ai7zOCBy74yRBoAbM-1uX_MTIub3JqbASx9d2yBt_iIByDCvhlex7yc' alt='' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Attribution on casualties: Reporting cited a Telegram post by Udmurt Republic health minister Sergei Bagin on injuries and hospitalisations after the strike.</li><li>Timing and framing: Ukraine’s General Staff said on Saturday that a missile strike hit what it described as a ballistic-missile manufacturing plant in the remote Udmurtia region.</li><li>Separate account details: Devdiscourse (citing The Telegraph) said long-range FP-5 Flamingo cruise missiles were used and named both the Votkinsk Machine Building Plant in Udmurtia and a natural-gas processing plant in Samara as targets.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukraine’s General Staff: Kyiv said it struck a Russian facility it described as a ballistic-missile manufacturer in the Udmurtia region. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/ukraine-strikes-ballistic-missile-producer-deep-inside-russia-kyiv-says'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Udmurt Republic health officials: The local health minister said the attack caused injuries and that some people were hospitalised, according to a Telegram post cited by The Hindu. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/ukraine-strikes-key-industrial-site-deep-inside-russia/article70661035.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Devdiscourse/The Telegraph (as cited): A separate account said the strike involved long-range FP-5 Flamingo cruise missiles and named both the Votkinsk plant and a gas-processing facility in Samara as targets. (<a href='https://www.devdiscourse.com/article/law-order/3812823-tensions-escalate-key-developments-in-ukraine-and-russia-conflict?amp'>Devdiscourse</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/ukraine-strikes-key-industrial-site-deep-inside-russia/article70661035.ece'>Ukraine strikes key industrial site deep inside Russia</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/ukraine-strikes-ballistic-missile-producer-deep-inside-russia-kyiv-says'>Ukraine strikes ballistic missile producer deep inside Russia, Kyiv says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.devdiscourse.com/article/law-order/3812823-tensions-escalate-key-developments-in-ukraine-and-russia-conflict?amp'>Ukrainian forces launch long-range FP-5 Flamingo cruise missiles, striking the Votkinsk Machine Building Plant in Votkinsk, Udmurtia, Russia. Another missile strikes a natural-gas processing plant in Samara Oblast. (The Telegraph)</a> - devdiscourse.com</li></ul>